WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.231 --> 00:00:01.591
-Guys, I want to quickly
mention, later this week,

00:00:01.591 --> 00:00:04.136
we're going to be kicking off
our newest Summer Reads

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.872
book club contest.
-Ooh.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.507
-We do this every year.
It's a lot of fun.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.375
I'm going to pick five books

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.244
that I'm thinking about --
thinking about reading.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.679
[ Laughter ]
-Thinking.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.981
-That's what makes this club
different than any other club.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.883
-Other clubs --
-I'm considering reading these.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.685
-Yeah. Other clubs,
people read the book.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.153
You think about it.
-That's correct.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.488
I'm thinking about possibly
reading these books.

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:23.956
Then I'm going to
have you guys vote

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.926
on which one we should all
read together.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.461
I don't want to have to read
all five of them.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.262
Then you got to go,
"Oh, yeah, that one's --"

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:32.232
No, we all vote together.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.966
We win together.
We lose together.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.134
[ Cheers ]

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:36.702
Maybe --

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:38.838
Can we do six books?
-Oh.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.908
-Can we do six?
It has to be five?

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.042
-You want to do six?
-We can do six?

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.244
-Go nuts, man.
-We might do six.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.277
-Half a doz.

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:46.612
-Half a dozen, man.
I don't know,

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.748
'cause there's one I'm, like,
kind of flip-flopping on.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.882
-Really?

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.650
-I'm not sure.
-You're not sure. So, six?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.219
Make it six, man.
It's your show.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.420
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.323
Live. Live life, man.
Live it up. Live it hard.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.591
-I want to make sure
we have every --

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.193
I like different
types of things.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.428
I like my --
-Comic books.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.830
-No.
-Cookbooks.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.832
-[ Chuckles ]
No, I like my mysteries.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:09.902
I like --
-Ooh. Histories?

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:10.970
Ghost --
-Memoirs --

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.738
"Mem-wah."
-"Mem-wahz."

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:16.543
-I like -- I like my kind of
summer romance books.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.345
-Ooh.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.913
Spicy.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:24.284
So I might throw in, like,
a little summer romance.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:27.286
I like a Y.A. book in there
every now and then.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:28.955
-Oh, yeah, man.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.124
-Keeps me feeling young, man.
-Yeah.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.325
On top of the pile, man.
-Yeah, I read --

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:35.061
I read while I --
-You read while you jog.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.395
Yeah, I love it.
I've seen you do it.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.797
You have the thing, the little
thing with the holder.

00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:40.633
-You saw me in Central Park?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.101
-I was doing that.
I had the contraption.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.370
-You were fast, man.
-Had the book in front of me.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.871
And I'm like,
"Why is everyone looking at me?

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:47.907
Leave me alone.
I'm just like you," you know?

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.010
Wednesday we're going to go down
the list of the books,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.278
the finalists.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.846
But that doesn't really
mean anything.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:54.880
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.549
Because that's
when the fun begins.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.817
-Yeah, the fun begins
on "Wedns."

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.786
-We'll announce
the five to six books.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.088
[ Laughter ]
-5 1/2, yeah.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.456
-And then I'll tell you
what they're all about.

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.792
Then we'll decide on which
is going to be the winner.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.595
And then, when will we
decide the winner?

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:10.896
By next week?

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.998
So you got like a week
and a half to figure it out.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:15.901
This is like --
You're on my schedule, right?

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.303
You don't have to decide
right now.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.638
-No, man, it's all good.
-Take your time.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.640
Take the weekend.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.174
Enjoy yourself.
Go, "You know what?

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:23.742
I was thinking about this,
but now I like this.

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:25.144
I'm telling you,
it's probably going to be

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.345
one of those rom-coms. Steamy.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:27.980
-Ooh, steamy.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.182
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:32.418
-I don't even know
if I've ever read one.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.553
-A rom-com book?

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.088
-No, one of those sex books.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.155
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.725
-Like with, like,
Fabio on the cover?

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.893
-No, like "50 Shades of Grey"
or whatever.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.162
-Oh, "50 Shades of Grey," yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.697
Yeah -- You like it?
It's a good book?

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.765
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.633
Maybe like on a Kindle
or something.

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:48.667
-Yeah, yeah.
You don't want people --

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.035
-I don't want to be
holding the book.

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:52.271
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:54.874
-If it's dirty stuff
on my Kindle,

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.242
that's up to me, you know?

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.011
If you're holding the book,
like, you know --

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.612
-You're reading
a, like, giant, dirty --

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.881
-"101 Ways to Do It."
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.983
Big picture book. Rude.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.751
-Stay away from that dude
in the subway, yeah.

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:07.186
Wearing my jogger's hat.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.055
-Yeah, "Kama Sutra," yeah.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.422
Run as fast as you can.

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:12.124
-"101 Ways to Do It."

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:13.859
What the hell is he doing?
Yeah, get a life.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:16.228
-"Trip to Bone Town"?
That's an awful book.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:17.397
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.831
-That was a good --
That was a good book.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.433
That was actually --
-That is a good book.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.967
-That had a twist ending
I did not see coming.

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.136
-Yeah, very twisty.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.904
[ Laughter ]

